Article 17
(1) Prevention of acts of violence against women and children as referred to in Article 16, shall be implemented by SKPD whose duties and functions are in the field of: Regional Regulation of HSU Regency Year 2016 Number 3 concerning Protection of Women and Children
a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. education;
d. manpower;
e. women's empowerment and child protection;
f. mental and spiritual matters; and
g. public peace and order.
(2) Prevention of acts of violence by SKPD as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented in an integrated and continuous manner based on the Regional Action Plan.

CHAPTER XII
INVESTIGATION
Article 33
(1) In addition to general investigation officials, investigation of criminal acts of violence against women and children in this Regional Regulation, Regional Regulation of HSU Regency Year 2016 Number 3 concerning Protection of Women and Children may also be conducted by Civil Servant Investigators (PPNS) as referred to in the Criminal Procedure Law.
(2) PPNS as referred to in paragraph (1), are certain civil servant officials within the Regional Government who are appointed by authorized officials in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.
(3) In carrying out investigation duties, PPNS as referred to in paragraph (2), are authorized to:
a. receive reports or complaints from a person regarding the existence of criminal acts of violence against women and children;
b. take first action at that time at the scene and conduct examination;
c. interrogate a suspect and examine the suspect's identity;
d. seize objects and/or documents;
e. take fingerprints and photograph a person;
f. summon persons to be heard and examined as suspects or witnesses;
g. bring in expert witnesses needed in connection with the examination of the case;
h. terminate the investigation after receiving instructions from the General Investigator that there is insufficient evidence, or the incident does not constitute a criminal act and subsequently through the General Investigator notify this matter to the Public Prosecutor, suspect or their family; and/or
i. take other actions necessary for the smooth investigation of criminal acts of violence against women and children, which according to law can be accounted for.
(4) PPNS as referred to in paragraph (2), shall notify the commencement of the investigation and submit the results of their investigation to the Public Prosecutor through the Investigation Official of the Police of the Republic of Indonesia, in accordance with the provisions stipulated in the Criminal Procedure Law.

